        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A rating of a body of water based on measurable physical, chemical, and biological characteristics. (MSH)
 Levels of water quality expected to render a body of water suitable for its designated use; criteria are based on specific levels of pollutants that would make the water harmful if used for drinking, swimming, farming, fish production, or industrial processes; includes state-adopted and EPA-approved ambient standards for water bodies. (CSP)
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0597680</skos:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C0597680</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Finding</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


